{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-61850e6e-85d0-4535-93e1-7fa96789fa8c","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-bbdfbe7a4c3f1df1","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9015-le72t40j/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9015-E002.md","content":"# Link registered model versions to producing runs\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers the Model Registry side of run lineage: registered model versions record a link back to the run that produced them, so that the run (and its parameters and metrics) can be identified from a registered model version and a comparison can be opened from the Model Registry. The linkage uses the registry's existing extension point for structured metadata on model versions.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Define and record the linkage from a registered model version to the run that produced it, using the existing model version metadata extension point (custom properties on ModelVersion entities exposed via the registry REST API).\n- Make the linkage available through the registry's existing REST API so consuming UIs can resolve the producing run for a model version.\n- Apply the linkage when model versions are registered from runs (the producing run is captured as part of registration).\n- No Dashboard UI changes in this epic; surfacing the link in the UI is handled by the Dashboard team separately.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a model version registered from a run, when the model version is read via the registry REST API, then the run that produced it is identifiable from the model version's metadata.\n- Given a model version with run linkage, when the linkage is resolved, then it points at a run that is accessible in the same project context (parameters and metrics of that run retrievable through existing run surfaces).\n- The linkage mechanism uses the existing model version metadata extension point and does not require a new registry data model migration beyond that extension point.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-2 (P1): Registered model versions link back to the run that produced them, so a comparison can be opened from the Model Registry — registry-side half covered by this epic (the Dashboard-side surfacing is a separate epic owned by the Dashboard team).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":28803,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-af5787c22a735c8d","agent_id":"a475ba2ed7e87fef2","session_id":"000d175c-8257-4923-ab3f-0ba108064e97","uuid":"8dcb3775-1d16-4ca9-956e-e5926a3e6037","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:50:30.200Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9015"}
