lable. |\n59\t| HLR-4 | P2 | RHAISTRAT-9015-E005 | Substantive documentation of a new workflow (new doc topics), a distinct work-product type → separate docs-authoring epic. |\n60\t\n61\t## Health Warnings\n62\t\n63\t- **Missing strategy sections (non-blocking):** The strategy provides the Affected Components as a bare list (no change/owner columns) and omits the Impacted Teams table, Dependencies table, Acceptance Criteria, and Non-Functional Requirements. Owner teams were inferred from the architecture-context files (`dashboard.md`, `model-registry.md`, `data-science-pipelines.md`). The docs epic has no team information in the strategy; it is assigned to a Documentation team by convention — verify with the strategy author.\n64\t- **Passive component classification:** Data Science Pipelines is listed as affected but the strategy describes no code change to it — per-run parameters and metrics are already surfaced in the Dashboard (problem statement) via the existing KFP v2 surface. It is classified passive; because a different team (RHOAI Pipelines) owns it, the passive-component exception generates a separate validation Implementation epic (RHAISTRAT-9015-E004) rather than only an acceptance criterion.\n65\t- **HLR redundancy:** HLR-1 and HLR-3 state one capability twice in different words (side-by-side view vs. diff of the same run data); consolidated into a single epic — see the HLR Traceability Matrix. Reviewers should confirm the customer councils' intent is fully captured by the combined scope.\n66\t- No priority inversions identified: P0 (core comparison surface) is the largest but well-precedented UI work; P1 epics extend it; docs at P1 per the docs-authoring priority exception (strategy frontmatter `priority: Major` → P1).\n67\t\n68\t## Tiered Delivery\n69\t\n70\tNot applicable. There are no external dependencies with uncertain timing; all work is in-platform. E001 delivers independent user value immediately (HLR-1/HLR-3) while the P1 epics proceed in parallel.\n71\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9c5fb85cbf9aabae","agent_id":"a96235dc186d39004","session_id":"000d175c-8257-4923-ab3f-0ba108064e97","uuid":"44f48569-626b-4e95-b4f7-44a71ceb9b24","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:52:40.201Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-89c57556682c91b9","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9015 decomposition"}
