parately.\n41\t\n42\t## Acceptance Criteria\n43\t\n44\t- Given a model version registered from a run, when the model version is read via the registry REST API, then the run that produced it is identifiable from the model version's metadata.\n45\t- Given a model version with run linkage, when the linkage is resolved, then it points at a run that is accessible in the same project context (parameters and metrics of that run retrievable through existing run surfaces).\n46\t- The linkage mechanism uses the existing model version metadata extension point and does not require a new registry data model migration beyond that extension point.\n47\t\n48\t## HLR Traceability\n49\t\n50\t- HLR-2 (P1): Registered model versions link back to the run that produced them, so a comparison can be opened from the Model Registry — registry-side half covered by this epic (the Dashboard-side surfacing is a separate epic owned by the Dashboard team).\n51\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9c5fb85cbf9aabae","agent_id":"a96235dc186d39004","session_id":"000d175c-8257-4923-ab3f-0ba108064e97","uuid":"89c00067-e8fb-404a-bf36-3ecfac765b8c","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:52:44.124Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8470eb623ae8e73b","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9015 decomposition"}
