tion is handled separately.\n43\t\n44\t## Acceptance Criteria\n45\t\n46\t- Given a registered model version that has a producing-run link, when the user views it in the Model Registry UI, then the producing run is visible and identifiable.\n47\t- Given a registered model version with a producing-run link, when the user opens a comparison from it, then the run comparison view opens with the producing run selected so a second run can be chosen for comparison.\n48\t- Given a registered model version without a producing-run link (legacy registrations), when viewed, then the comparison entry point degrades gracefully without errors.\n49\t- The entry point reuses the existing run comparison view rather than duplicating it.\n50\t\n51\t## HLR Traceability\n52\t\n53\t- HLR-2 (P1): Registered model versions link back to the run that produced them, so a comparison can be opened from the Model Registry — Dashboard-side half covered by this epic (registry-side linkage is a separate epic owned by the Model Registry team).\n54\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9c5fb85cbf9aabae","agent_id":"a96235dc186d39004","session_id":"000d175c-8257-4923-ab3f-0ba108064e97","uuid":"c94066f9-79e8-43b8-9e0f-63b7ab668805","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:52:44.710Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9d2a9268e2d1e928","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9015 decomposition"}
